<title>CANADA: Ariel wins Costa Rica environment approval.</title>
<headline>Ariel wins Costa Rica environment approval.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ariel Resources Ltd said on Tuesday that its environmental impact study for an open pit gold mine in Costa Rica has been approved.</p>
<p>The Costa Rican Ministry of Energy and the Environment notified the company of the approval today, Ariel said in a statement.</p>
<p>Approval for the Fortuna pit at Ariel's San Martin mine is subject to the company making the required deposit guarantee within 30 days, the company said.</p>
<p>Ariel agreed earlier this month to merge its operations with Dakota Mining Corp.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau 416-941-8100</p>
</text>
